{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520810-al-aswad","id":1520810,"title":"Al Aswad","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-17T06:46:11-07:00","id":1520810,"title":"Al Aswad","content":"I haven been reading up a bit on the black one who appears in the book of madness. i wondering where you guys would rank him powerwise compared to say the likes of ur shulgi, nergal or even the antediluviaans. i think with prep he can take anybody on! Including Caine! but i am not sure how he would fare in a white room fight scenario against a truly powerful vampire because as a mage he is obviously less durable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T12:16:11-07:00","id":1520830,"title":"","content":"I think the question is fairly meaningless. The man is a stand-in for Satan on earth. Even though he is given stats, as one of the Dark Lords he is clearly in ST fiat territory as a storytelling device. His counterparts among the Dark Lords are either not given stats, or given stats merely for one of their &quot;major manifestations.&quot; We should proceed cautiously.<br /> <br /> Any combat scenario would degenerate into STs making very difficult decisions on interpreting game mechanics that are meant to be nebulous and open to ST interpretation as a storytelling device. How do you interpret stats like Arcane 7 or Destiny 8? What kind of astonishing insights against your opponent can you get with Dream 5? What kind of things can you do with Entropy 6? What stats are you going to assign the antedeluvians or Caine since those are not detailed? An ST could argue Al-Aswad is simply incapable of being killed by any vampire, and it would be hard to argue. Or another ST who assigns all sorts of incomparable powers to Caine would argue of course he could destroy Al-Aswad. It just comes down to personal preference and how an ST wants their chronicle setting to be like.<br /> <br /> I would say he is meant to be more powerful than any legitimate character who has &quot;real&quot; stats. And that he is at the same level of general power as other characters who are only really meant as storytelling tools.<br /> <br /> For me personally and how I view the setting, Al-Aswad is the kind of character who shows up in a later stage of the Apocalypse when Gehenna is mostly resolved and the surviving antedeluvians are facing off against the other great terrors of the world on a mostly ravaged Earth where the living envy the dead. RPG mechanics no longer apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T22:51:02-07:00","id":1520855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520810-al-aswad#post1520810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including Caine!</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth to mention, Caine's &quot;invulnerability&quot; was never his Disciplines - if he even had any. He wasn't even dead, nor a vampire for that matter<br /> The only &quot;facts&quot; about him are from the book of nod and those fragments are really debatable sources at best, even the Noddist can't agree in interpretations<br /> And only there there is a passing mention about Caine's powers, and even in that, it is said:<br /> &quot;Looking around me, I knew that I had Awakened.&quot;<br /> When my energies first surged through me I discovered how to move like lightning - this some interpet as Celerity<br /> how to borrow the strength of the earth - this some interpet as Potence<br /> how to be as stone - this some interpet as Fortitude<br /> Lilith then showed me how she hides herself from hunters - this some interpet as Obfuscate<br /> how she commands obedience - this some interpet as Dominate<br /> and how she demands respect - this some interpet as Presence<br /> Then, Awakening myself further, I found the way to alter forms - this some interpet as Protean<br /> the way to have dominion over animals - this some interpet as Animalism<br /> the way to make eyes see sight - this some interpet as Auspex<br /> [...]<br /> and saw the infinite possibilities in the stars and knew that a path of power, a path of Blood - and this some interpet as the thaumaturgical Path of Blood<br /> <br /> But the Book of Nood is the collection of fragments from pottery bits, things carved on bones, stone tablets, oral history and basically anything that could fit in<br /> Heck it is worse than the Bible that is a collection of old hebrew text and &quot;gospels&quot; centuries later, heavly edited and cherry picked, thats why only four there, not all of them - what not fit in, left out<br /> <br /> Caine was never Embraced, nor died.. the curses are not actually from God, even the Book of Nod credited them to the Archangles<br /> <br /> &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot; - Michael<br /> <br /> &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always. Hide now for the Sun rises to take its wrath on you.&quot; - Raphael<br /> <br /> &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness You will drink only blood You will eat only ashes. You will be always as you were at death, Never dying, living on. You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.&quot; - Uriel<br /> <br /> &quot;Son of Adam, Son of Eve, Behold, the mercy of the Father is greater than you can ever know for even now there is a path opened a road of Mercy and you shall call this road Golconda&quot; - Gabriel<br /> <br /> Funny to mention, these are not only for the &quot;undead&quot; descendats, but the Children of Caine<br /> Any Children, actually - witch opens up a whole lot of possibilites<br /> <br /> Then when he turned Enoch, Urial added another:<br /> <br /> &quot;Cain, although you are powerful, and marked of God,know this: that any son that you do will bear your curse, any of its progeny will forever in the Land of Nod and fear of the flame and the sun, only drink blood and eat only ashes.And as they take the seed of jealousy of their father,they always conspire and fight each other.Do not condemn these grandchildren of Adam who seek the path honored&quot;<br /> <br /> Lets put aside, several of the curses on close inspeiton just fall apart, like the whole eat ash part, but move on<br /> Caine was &quot;famous&quot; with his deal with Demons, actually he was the first Infernalist and had a fair share of deals with them and his curses are legendary - again, by the account of the Book of Nod<br /> <br /> But Caine power never lied with the Awakened powers - that could be anything<br /> No the deals and knowledge he gained from demons<br /> Caine's main and basically only power was the Sevenfold Curse - , if someone harmed Cain, the damage would come back sevenfold.<br /> And the Mark - God's promise to offer Cain divine protection from premature death (i.e untill God wants him to die) with the stated purpose of preventing anyone from killing him. It is not known what the mark was, but it is assumed that the mark was visible<br /> <br /> So the Mark and the Sevenfold Curse the actuall thing that prevents Caine from &quot;losing&quot; in any scenario<br /> Literally untill God Almighty don't wan't him to die... he will not and and harm will be reflected back seven times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:20:30-07:00","id":1520862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520810-al-aswad?p=1520855#post1520855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So the Mark and the Sevenfold Curse the actuall thing that prevents Caine from &quot;losing&quot; in any scenario<br /> Literally untill God Almighty don't wan't him to die... he will not and and harm will be reflected back seven times</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anybody even tested the sevenfold curse? sounds like a convenient curse to say you have just so nobody tries to kill you! Even assuming its true, there are worst fates then death. A creature like Al Aswad could potentiaal banish him to a dimension worse then hell! he may wish he could die then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T05:06:13-07:00","id":1520872,"title":"","content":"Well, the Unnamed's power always was in his mind. His knowledge, wisdom, patience, and strategic mind. NOT his admittedly great powers<br /> He always urged caution, only to show mankind the way to ruin the world, not lead them, seeing himself as a father who helped his children, humanity, to achieve their full destructive potential.<br /> While his stats are awesome, for sure... he never actually did anything &quot;famous&quot; - I mean anything that would talk about his powers<br /> And when the Consensus shifted even he found that it became more and more difficult for him to access the Tapestry, as he was too intertwined with the Outer Darkness. To ensure the continuation of his plan, he gave twenty Nephandi his knowledge in 313 BCE before he departed into the Void, resting and amassing his power while watching Creation from the outside.<br /> His main power I think lied indeed his wisdom, he relaised that the fragments of the One would never unite - esepcialyl not against him.<br /> While he gathered enough powert to made his way back into existence and created the Tenth Seat<br /> Every victory he earned was becasue of the arrogance, hubris, self-congratulatory worldviews and and his enemies own petty disagreements. Ultimately that led to their defeats<br /> He was basically Thrawn<br /> Brilliant, tactical mind and used every advatage to achieve is victories without Thrawn nobility and honor<br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but his greatest feat was to force the Avatar Storm through the Gauntlet - but he needed the souls of his challangers who were defeatd becasue what I mentioned above. And he manipulated them from the start to the end<br /> Sure, following that using the tainted Quintessence harvested from the Storm and Horizon he &quot;killed&quot; the Alder Bole, the World Tree<br /> But tehcnically, while this was an awesome spell and feat, all of those built upon strategy, planning and the fact he realized the weakness of the potential enemies<br /> What Black Fox said about him and how he view the setting, Al-Aswad to the kind of character who shows up in a later stage of the Apocalypse when Gehenna is mostly resolved and the surviving antedeluvians are facing off against the other great terrors of the world on a mostly ravaged Earth where the living envy the dead?<br /> Yes<br /> Totally in his character... and actually that was what he essentiall done always in his exitence<br /> The things you mentioned rarely was given stats becasue... well... they are like him are tools<br /> But realistically speaking, in a white room scenario he ineed have stats and having them is limtiing him<br /> Ur-Shulgi, Antediluvians or Caine, Lilith, Lucifer or any Archduke of the Fallen, Yama King aiming he seat of the Demon Emperor... don't have any thus could be anything in the hands of the storyteller.<br /> But if you compare stats, with lets say Nergal/Huitzilopochtli, cosidering the Baali's stats, knowledge, lores and everything listed... he probably would win against Al-Aswad<br /> His two versions: (Qlippothic) Correspondence 6, Entropy 10, Forces 5, Life 5, Matter 5, Mind 7, Prime 8, Spirit 8, Time 5 or Correspondence 4, Entropy 6, Forces 5, Life 4, Matter 4, Mind 4, Prime 4, Spirit 5, Time 5 - epending the edtion you would use falls flat against Nergal/Huitzilopochtli's skills, knowledge disciplines and backgrounds even with the added Arcane 7, Avatar 9, Destiny 8, Dream 5 or limitless qiintessence<br /> Remember, while he defeated the Awakened &quot;chalangers&quot; at Horizon that mostly was a one-on-one battle, not swarm of mages (tho probbaly could deal with them) BUT when he faced with a small cabal of mages that had managed to recover the Greater Parma Magica (and with the help of Senex, who managed to wound him seriously), the Unnamed was forced to <i>flee</i><br /> He was not omnipotent, nor omniscient got wounded and fled<br /> He is a powerfull tool in the ST box, yes, and very few PC would be able to win against him (*cough* Paws of the Newborn Cub *cough* a Rank 5 Silverfang would be enough, or a pack of them, if you want to be sure) several other similar powerhouses like him? Yes<br /> And of course as the story requires<br /> \u200bSo while he question is indeed interesting and we could argue endlessly who whould win, ultimately the answer: whover you want in your chronicle to win","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-18-2023, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T05:30:17-07:00","id":1520937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520810-al-aswad#post1520810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven been reading up a bit on the black one who appears in the book of madness. i wondering where you guys would rank him powerwise compared to say the likes of ur shulgi, nergal or even the antediluviaans. i think with prep he can take anybody on! Including Caine! but i am not sure how he would fare in a white room fight scenario against a truly powerful vampire because as a mage he is obviously less durable!</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you consider taking his faction or his team ( the Nephandi, or some magical beings, or maybe some mercenary Tradition Mages ? ) into account with this ? A particular character's team or group certainly matters and is very important in a fictional setting.<br /> <br /> I have to say that both comic books and normal literature are excellent sources in regard to duels, challanges, and ongoing wars or feuds. More traditional legends and myths - including traditional storytelling, singing, oratory, and tales - are also definitely worthwhile and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}